#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:1
msgid "Streams Working Group"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:3
msgid ""
"The Node.js Streams is jointly governed by a Working Group (WG) that is "
"responsible for high-level guidance of the project."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:7
msgid "The WG has final authority over this project including:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:9
msgid "Technical direction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:10
msgid "Project governance and process (including this policy)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:11
msgid "Contribution policy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:12
msgid "GitHub repository hosting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:13
msgid "Conduct guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:14
msgid "Maintaining the list of additional Collaborators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:16
msgid ""
"For the current list of WG members, see the project "
"[README.md](./README.md#current-project-team-members)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:19
msgid "Collaborators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:21
msgid ""
"The readable-stream GitHub repository is maintained by the WG and "
"additional Collaborators who are added by the WG on an ongoing basis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:25
msgid ""
"Individuals making significant and valuable contributions are made "
"Collaborators and given commit-access to the project. These individuals "
"are identified by the WG and their addition as Collaborators is discussed"
" during the WG meeting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:30
msgid ""
"_Note:_ If you make a significant contribution and are not considered for"
" commit-access log an issue or contact a WG member directly and it will "
"be brought up in the next WG meeting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:34
msgid ""
"Modifications of the contents of the readable-stream repository are made "
"on a collaborative basis. Anybody with a GitHub account may propose a "
"modification via pull request and it will be considered by the project "
"Collaborators. All pull requests must be reviewed and accepted by a "
"Collaborator with sufficient expertise who is able to take full "
"responsibility for the change. In the case of pull requests proposed by "
"an existing Collaborator, an additional Collaborator is required for "
"sign-off. Consensus should be sought if additional Collaborators "
"participate and there is disagreement around a particular modification. "
"See _Consensus Seeking Process_ below for further detail on the consensus"
" model used for governance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:47
msgid ""
"Collaborators may opt to elevate significant or controversial "
"modifications, or modifications that have not found consensus to the WG "
"for discussion by assigning the ***WG-agenda*** tag to a pull request or "
"issue. The WG should serve as the final arbiter where required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:53
msgid ""
"For the current list of Collaborators, see the project "
"[README.md](./README.md#members)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:56
msgid "WG Membership"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:58
msgid ""
"WG seats are not time-limited.  There is no fixed size of the WG. "
"However, the expected target is between 6 and 12, to ensure adequate "
"coverage of important areas of expertise, balanced with the ability to "
"make decisions efficiently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:63
msgid ""
"There is no specific set of requirements or qualifications for WG "
"membership beyond these rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:66
msgid "The WG may add additional members to the WG by unanimous consensus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:68
msgid ""
"A WG member may be removed from the WG by voluntary resignation, or by "
"unanimous consensus of all other WG members."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:71
msgid ""
"Changes to WG membership should be posted in the agenda, and may be "
"suggested as any other agenda item (see \"WG Meetings\" below)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:74
msgid ""
"If an addition or removal is proposed during a meeting, and the full WG "
"is not in attendance to participate, then the addition or removal is "
"added to the agenda for the subsequent meeting.  This is to ensure that "
"all members are given the opportunity to participate in all membership "
"decisions.  If a WG member is unable to attend a meeting where a planned "
"membership decision is being made, then their consent is assumed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:82
msgid ""
"No more than 1/3 of the WG members may be affiliated with the same "
"employer.  If removal or resignation of a WG member, or a change of "
"employment by a WG member, creates a situation where more than 1/3 of the"
" WG membership shares an employer, then the situation must be immediately"
" remedied by the resignation or removal of one or more WG members "
"affiliated with the over-represented employer(s)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:89
msgid "WG Meetings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:91
msgid ""
"The WG meets occasionally on a Google Hangout On Air. A designated "
"moderator approved by the WG runs the meeting. Each meeting should be "
"published to YouTube."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:95
msgid ""
"Items are added to the WG agenda that are considered contentious or are "
"modifications of governance, contribution policy, WG membership, or "
"release process."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:99
msgid ""
"The intention of the agenda is not to approve or review all patches; that"
" should happen continuously on GitHub and be handled by the larger group "
"of Collaborators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:103
msgid ""
"Any community member or contributor can ask that something be added to "
"the next meeting's agenda by logging a GitHub Issue. Any Collaborator, WG"
" member or the moderator can add the item to the agenda by adding the "
"***WG-agenda*** tag to the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:108
msgid ""
"Prior to each WG meeting the moderator will share the Agenda with members"
" of the WG. WG members can add any items they like to the agenda at the "
"beginning of each meeting. The moderator and the WG cannot veto or remove"
" items."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:113
msgid ""
"The WG may invite persons or representatives from certain projects to "
"participate in a non-voting capacity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:116
msgid ""
"The moderator is responsible for summarizing the discussion of each "
"agenda item and sends it as a pull request after the meeting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:119
msgid "Consensus Seeking Process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:121
msgid ""
"The WG follows a [Consensus Seeking](http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki"
"/Consensus-seeking_decision-making) decision-making model."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:126
msgid ""
"When an agenda item has appeared to reach a consensus the moderator will "
"ask \"Does anyone object?\" as a final call for dissent from the "
"consensus."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:130
msgid ""
"If an agenda item cannot reach a consensus a WG member can call for "
"either a closing vote or a vote to table the issue to the next meeting. "
"The call for a vote must be seconded by a majority of the WG or else the "
"discussion will continue. Simple majority wins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/readable-stream_GOVERNANCE.md:135
msgid ""
"Note that changes to WG membership require a majority consensus.  See "
"\"WG Membership\" above."
msgstr ""

